# Applies to every build whose context is the repo root: apps/app/Dockerfile.web (the
# docker-compose and CI frontend build) and fly/Dockerfile (via `flyctl deploy`).
#
# Why this file has to exist. BuildKit reads .dockerignore from the *context root*, and
# both Dockerfiles are rooted here. With nothing to exclude, two things happen, both
# measured on this repo:
#
#   1. The context balloons.        15.85 kB / 0.3s  ->  38.74 MB / 25.8s
#   2. A `COPY` of a workspace overlays the host's node_modules on top of the one
#      `npm ci` just built INSIDE the image. Node resolves the nearest node_modules
#      first, so the host copy then wins — and a host-built native binary would be the
#      wrong platform for the image.
#
# Do NOT exclude backend/, packages/ or fly/ — all three are copied by fly/Dockerfile.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# Test/build output
apps/app/test-results
apps/app/playwright-report
apps/app/e2e/.auth
apps/app/.expo
apps/app/android
apps/app/ios

# Local runtime state — the DB is a Fly volume in production
# Patterns without **/ only match at the context root, so `data` alone never covered
# backend/data, where the dev stack keeps a copy of the production database
# (prod-snapshot/) and the dev JWT secret. `flyctl deploy` uploads this context.
**/data/
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/prod-snapshot
**/.dev-jwt

# Docs and design assets: nothing in any image reads these
docs
design
releases
**/*.md
!README.md
